<title>USA: Maine regulators approve lower workers' comp rates.</title>
<headline>Maine regulators approve lower workers' comp rates.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Maine insurance regulators approved a 12.5 percent drop in the cost of worker's compensation insurance, which will cut premiums for insured employers by $20 million if insurers adopt the new rates.</p>
<p>&quot;Combined with other recent reductions, this means that workers' compensation rates have fallen almost 32 percent over the last three years, making Maine more competitive for new business and new jobs,&quot; said Gov. Angus King in prepared remarks.</p>
<p>However, some lawmakers are questioning whether injured workers are really paying for the savings, and have introduced legislation to change portions of the state worker's compensation laws that have led to the rate decreases.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650))</p>
